VERSION 18

*******************************************************************************
*** WaterHeating - Example 1 of the curated TRNSYS 19 example set.
***
*** A stratified water tank (Type 158, 5 isothermal nodes) with an immersed
*** auxiliary heater controlled by a thermostat (Type 2).  A constant load
*** draws water from the bottom and returns cold water to the top.  No
*** external data files, no weather, no schedules - the smallest realistic
*** feedback-control system the kernel can run.
***
*** Components:
***   Type 158 (Tank)        - 5 nodes, one thermostat, one aux heater
***   Type 2   (Thermostat)  - on/off control with hysteresis
***   Type 65  (Plotter)     - tank temps + control signal
***
*** Expected behavior: tank starts cold (20 C), heater fires to drive the
*** tank toward setpoint (60 C), then cycles through hysteresis as the
*** constant load extracts heat.  Plot shows the temperature rise, the
*** on/off heater pattern, and the steady-state oscillation around setpoint.
***
*** This deck is also the demo target for TypeDev: a TypeDev installation
*** can override Type 2 with a custom thermostat (MyType2) to change the
*** control logic.  Load order (user-list shadows bundled) determines which
*** Type 2 actually loads at simulation time.
*******************************************************************************

CONSTANTS 3
START = 0
STOP  = 48
STEP  = 0.125

SIMULATION START STOP STEP
TOLERANCES 0.001 0.001
LIMITS 30 30 30
DFQ 1
WIDTH 80
LIST
SOLVER 0 1 1
NAN_CHECK 0
OVERWRITE_CHECK 0
TIME_REPORT 0
EQSOLVER 1

EQUATIONS 6
T_set    = 60
T_amb    = 20
Q_aux    = 5000              ! kJ/h, full heater power
m_load   = 8                 ! kg/h, constant load extraction
T_cold   = 15                ! C, cold-water inlet to the tank
Q_heater = [2,1] * Q_aux     ! Type 2's control signal scaled to heater power

UNIT 1 TYPE 158	 Tank
PARAMETERS 17
0.3		! 1  Tank volume [m3]
1.5		! 2  Tank height [m]
5		! 3  Number of tank nodes
2.5		! 4  Top loss coefficient [kJ/h.m2.K]
2.5		! 5  Edge loss coefficient [kJ/h.m2.K]
2.5		! 6  Bottom loss coefficient [kJ/h.m2.K]
4.19		! 7  Fluid specific heat [kJ/kg.K]
1000		! 8  Fluid density [kg/m3]
2.224		! 9  Fluid thermal conductivity [kJ/h.m.K]
1.0		! 10 Height fraction of inlet 1 (cold water in at top)
0.0		! 11 Height fraction of outlet 1 (hot water out at bottom)
0.0		! 12 Height fraction of inlet 2 (unused)
1.0		! 13 Height fraction of outlet 2 (unused)
1		! 14 Number of thermostats
0.5		! 15 Height fraction of thermostat 1 (mid-tank)
1		! 16 Number of auxiliary heat inputs
0.5		! 17 Height fraction of aux heater 1 (mid-tank)
INPUTS 8
T_cold		! Inlet temperature port 1 (cold water replacing draw)
m_load		! Inlet flow rate port 1
0,0		! Inlet temperature port 2 (unused)
0,0		! Inlet flow rate port 2 (unused)
T_amb		! Top loss temperature
T_amb		! Edge loss temperature
T_amb		! Bottom loss temperature
Q_heater	! Aux heater power (kJ/h) - control signal scaled by Q_aux via EQUATIONS
*** INITIAL INPUT VALUES
15. 50. 20. 0. 20. 20. 20. 0.
DERIVATIVES 5
20.
20.
20.
20.
20.
*** Five nodes all start at 20 C.

UNIT 2 TYPE 2	 Thermostat
PARAMETERS 2
10		! 1 NSTK - sticking-check count (Solver 0)
90		! 2 Tmax - max-temp shutoff threshold [C]
INPUTS 6
T_set		! T1 - upper input (setpoint signal)
1,14		! T2 - lower input (tank temp at thermostat, Type 158 output 14)
1,14		! T3 - monitoring temperature for max-temp cutoff
0,0		! Incoming control function (initial state 0 = off)
0,0		! Upper dead band - switch ON when T1 - T2 > 5 (tank < setpoint - 5)
0,0		! Lower dead band - switch OFF when T1 - T2 < 0 (tank > setpoint)
*** INITIAL INPUT VALUES
60. 20. 20. 0. 5. 0.
*** First output of Type 2 (output 1) is the control signal, scaled below
*** to drive the tank's aux heater input.  When standard Type 2 is loaded
*** the control follows hysteresis.  When MyType2 (TypeDev override) is
*** loaded its own logic runs in this Unit's place.

UNIT 3 TYPE 65	 Plotter
PARAMETERS 12
4		! 1  Nb. of left-axis variables (temperatures)
1		! 2  Nb. of right-axis variables (control signal)
0		! 3  Left axis minimum
100		! 4  Left axis maximum
0		! 5  Right axis minimum
1		! 6  Right axis maximum
1		! 7  Number of plots per simulation
7		! 8  X-axis gridpoints
0		! 9  Shut off online w/o removing
-1		! 10 Logical unit for output file
0		! 11 Output file units
0		! 12 Output file delimiter
INPUTS 5
1,5		! Tank average
1,14		! Thermostat reading
T_set		! Setpoint reference line
T_amb		! Ambient reference line
2,1		! Type 2 control signal (right axis)
*** INITIAL INPUT VALUES
T_avg T_thermostat T_set T_ambient control
LABELS 3
"Temperature [C]"
"Control [0/1]"
"Tank with thermostat-controlled heater"

END
